<http://data.silknow.org/object/342bea6a-f967-3b49-97ae-ad0e0bc98c56>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Brocaded silk; Italy; 1760s"@en , "Brocade woven in silk and silver thread on a taffeta silk ground. The pattern consists of wavy band (in red) imitating lace, with roses in silver or green, white, and shades of red and blue. Between the bands is a repeating pattern of a man, cap in hand, offering a bouquet to a lady with a large parasol, behind whom a dog is standing on his hind legs. These figures are in colours and are shown standing on a silver ground. The ground of the brocade is salmon-coloured."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/c6c26078-2191-322d-ad6a-3a3deb1b9bc2> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Brocaded silk; Italy; 1760s"@en , "Brocade woven in silk and silver thread on a taffeta silk ground. The pattern consists of wavy band (in red) imitating lace, with roses in silver or green, white, and shades of red and blue. Between the bands is a repeating pattern of a man, cap in hand, offering a bouquet to a lady with a large parasol, behind whom a dog is standing on his hind legs. These figures are in colours and are shown standing on a silver ground. The ground of the brocade is salmon-coloured."@en ;
